# Polyglot — environment template
#
# Copy to .env and fill in real values. .env is gitignored (*.env in
# .gitignore); this file (.env.example) is the tracked template.
# .env.local is for per-developer overrides on top of .env (also gitignored).
#
# Loaded by the Makefile (include .env) so every `make` target sees these
# as exported env vars. The Go app itself should also load .env at startup
# (internal/config/config.go — TODO: wire a loader like joho/godotenv or
# read env directly; until then, set these in the shell that runs `make run`).

# ─── PostgreSQL (app database + migration target) ──────────────────────
# Defaults below match deployments/docker-compose.yml so `make db-up &&
# make migrate-up` works out of the box. Override in .env for production.
POSTGRES_HOST=localhost
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
POSTGRES_USER=postgres
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=netops
POSTGRES_DB=netops
# Full connection string consumed by golang-migrate and the app. Built from
# the vars above — override only if you need a non-standard sslmode or
# multiple pools (e.g. sslmode=require for managed Postgres).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:netops@localhost:5432/netops?sslmode=disable

# ─── Credential Vault (AES-GCM key for encrypting device credentials) ──
# The credentials table stores an AES-GCM ciphertext blob (see migration
# 000001). This key encrypts/decrypts it. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# NEVER commit a real key — .env is gitignored, but double-check.
POLYGLOT_VAULT_KEY=

# ─── Integration test: Mikrotik (real CHR/device in GNS3) ──────────────
# Absent → test/integration/mikrotik_test.go skips (build tag "integration").
MIKROTIK_TEST_HOST=
MIKROTIK_TEST_USER=
MIKROTIK_TEST_PASS=

# ─── Integration test: GenieACS NBI ────────────────────────────────────
# Point at a real GenieACS instance reachable from CI/dev. Absent → skip.
# GENIEACS_TEST_URL format: http://host:port (no trailing slash).
# GENIEACS_TEST_DEVICE_ID: a device ID that exists in that GenieACS instance
#   and is safe to run read-only tasks against (getParameterValues).
GENIEACS_TEST_URL=
GENIEACS_TEST_DEVICE_ID=
GENIEACS_TEST_API_KEY=

# ─── Testcontainers (Go integration tests that spin up Docker) ────────
# testcontainers-go talks to the Docker daemon directly — no DB credentials
# needed here. Override the image only if you need a specific Postgres
# version for schema-compat testing.
TESTCONTAINERS_POSTGRES_IMAGE=postgres:17-alpine

# ─── MCP Server (transport + demo device) ─────────────────────────────
# Transport: "stdio" (LibreChat spawns Go binary as subprocess) or "http"
# (Go binary serves MCP on an HTTP endpoint, default :8080/mcp).
MCP_TRANSPORT=http
MCP_HTTP_ADDR=:8080

# Demo device — optional. When set, the in-memory repository loads one
# device at startup so MCP tools can be tested end-to-end without a
# database. Replace with Postgres-backed repository when that adapter lands.
# POLYGLOT_DEMO_EXTRA_* vars become entries in device.Extra (e.g.
# POLYGLOT_DEMO_EXTRA_use_tls=true for GenieACS HTTPS).
POLYGLOT_DEMO_DEVICE_ID=
POLYGLOT_DEMO_DRIVER_TYPE=mikrotik
POLYGLOT_DEMO_HOST=
POLYGLOT_DEMO_PORT=
POLYGLOT_DEMO_USERNAME=
POLYGLOT_DEMO_PASSWORD=
